      "title": "Low velocity, high pressure: gentle on alumina",
      "description": "In dense phase the blow tank is pressurised (often ~ 2–6 bar) and the alumina moves as slow plugs or dunes (typically ~ 2–10 m/s) rather than suspended at high speed. This greatly reduces particle breakage (attrition creates fines/dust that smelters dislike) and pipe wear, and needs less air than dilute-phase conveying.",
